DVSM INDUSTRIAL META-KERNEL v1.1 (SMOKEPLATE COMPATIBLE FINAL ADDENDUM)
===============================================================================

AUTHOR BLOCK / PROVENANCE / INTELLECTUAL FRAMEWORK NOTICE
============================================================

PROJECT:
DVSM :: Industrial Meta-Kernel v1.1
Deterministic Distributed Execution + Multi-Scale Invariant Consensus System

AUTHOR:
Daniel J. Dillberg

LICENSE:
GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 (AGPL-3.0)

CLASSIFICATION:
Formal Deterministic Distributed Execution Specification

PROTECTED PRIMITIVES:
- Ξ Execution Kernel
- S_ECHO Invariant Identity Functor
- RENORMALIZE Projection Operator
- L5 Consensus Attractor Engine
- Event Algebra (⊕, →, ℛ)
- EventIR Typed Representation
- SHA256 Staged Folding Pipeline

SMOKEPLATE COMPATIBILITY:
This build introduces controlled implementation variance tolerance across heterogeneous compute environments while preserving strict invariant equivalence in S_ECHO space.

===============================================================================
SYSTEM STATUS
===============================================================================

STATUS:
Formal Protocol Specification / Deterministic Distributed Execution System

PRIMARY OBJECTIVE:

Define a deterministic system where:

    STATE(t+1) = Ξ(INPUT(t), STATE(t))

and correctness is defined not locally, but through global convergence:

    REALITY = CONSENSUS(S_ECHO(STATE))

NOTE:
Consensus is NOT final authority. It is a convergence detector operating over invariant state projections.

===============================================================================
SMOKEPLATE DESIGN PRINCIPLE
===============================================================================

Smokeplate mode permits variability in execution substrate:

- CPU / GPU / SIMD / WASM divergence
- memory layout differences
- alignment and padding variation
- floating-point backend substitution (if normalized)

CONSTRAINT:

    S_ECHO(Event_A) == S_ECHO(Event_B)

MUST remain invariant.

Thus:
- execution may vary
- identity may not

===============================================================================
CORE EXECUTION MODEL
===============================================================================

Ξ (EXECUTION KERNEL)

    STATE(t+1) = Ξ(STATE(t), INPUT(t))

Properties:
- deterministic per L3 ordered input stream
- bitwise reproducible within canonical execution path
- no probabilistic branching in authoritative mode

L3 (TOTAL ORDER BROADCAST)

Defines causal sequence:

    τ ∈ ℤ⁺

All nodes observe identical event ordering.

L4 (PROOF GATE)

Validates:

    S_ECHO(RENORMALIZE(EVENT))

Rejects non-canonical or non-invariant events.

L5 (CONSENSUS ATTRACTOR)

Operates over invariant space:

    Σ(S_ECHO(EVENTS)) → stable fixed point

Consensus is convergence, not authority.

===============================================================================
RENORMALIZATION FUNCTOR
===============================================================================

RENORMALIZE(EVENT) produces invariant projection:

Fields:
- causal_type_id
- sequence_epoch (τ)
- origin_cell (quantized spatial domain)
- effect_signature (state delta hash)
- entropy_bound (ε-clamped noise limit)

Purpose:
Maps microstate execution into macro-invariant identity space.

Noise Rule:
Microstate variance is discarded if outside invariant projection space.

===============================================================================
S_ECHO IDENTITY FUNCTION
===============================================================================

Definition:

    S_ECHO(E) = SHA256(RENORMALIZE(E))

Interpretation:
Identity is equivalence class membership, not raw bit identity.

Rule:

    S_A == S_B  ⇔  S_ECHO(A) == S_ECHO(B)

===============================================================================
EVENT ALGEBRA SYSTEM
===============================================================================

EVENT SPACE:

    E ∈ EventSpace

All events are closed under invariant projection.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
⊕ COMPOSITION

    E3 = E1 ⊕ E2

Constraint:
- must respect L3 ordering adjacency

Property:

    RENORMALIZE(E1 ⊕ E2) =
        MERGE(RENORMALIZE(E1), RENORMALIZE(E2))

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
→ CAUSAL DEPENDENCY

    E1 → E2

Meaning:
- E2 depends on invariant state of E1

Constraint:
    τ(E2) > τ(E1)

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ℛ RECONSTRUCTION

    ℛ(S) = REPLAY(L3_STREAM)

Truth is recomputed, never stored.

Snapshots are invalid as authoritative state.

===============================================================================
EVENT IR (EIR) STRUCTURE
===============================================================================

Canonical EventIR (fixed ABI layout):

struct EventIR {
    uint16  type_id;
    uint64  sequence_epoch;
    uint64  origin_cell_hash;
    uint64  effect_signature;
    int64   entropy_bound;
    uint64  payload_size;
    uint64  payload_offset;
    uint64  reserved_flags;
};

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
TYPE SYSTEM

0x01 INPUT_COMMAND
0x02 PHYSICS_DELTA
0x03 STATE_MUTATION
0x04 NETWORK_MESSAGE
0x05 CONSENSUS_SIGNAL
0x06 ROLLBACK_MARKER
0x07 PROOF_ATTESTATION
0x08 NOISE_OBSERVATION (non-executing)
0x09 RENORMALIZATION_ANCHOR

===============================================================================
SMOKEPLATE FLAGS (reserved_flags)
===============================================================================

bit 0 → SMOKEPLATE_MODE_ENABLED
bit 1 → ALIGNMENT_FLEX_ALLOWED
bit 2 → FLOATING_POINT_TOLERANCE
bit 3 → SIMD_VARIANT_ALLOWED
bit 4 → GPU_EXECUTION_ALLOWED
bit 5 → NON_CANONICAL_PADDING_ALLOWED

RULE:
These flags never affect S_ECHO output.

===============================================================================
BINARY SERIALIZATION FORMAT (DVSM-BIN v1)
===============================================================================

Layout:

[ HEADER 64 bytes ]
[ PAYLOAD variable ]
[ FOOTER 32 bytes ]

FOOTER:

- CRC64 payload integrity
- invariant_hash_low
- invariant_hash_high
- S_ECHO binding tag

===============================================================================
HASH SCHEDULE (STAGED FOLDING PIPELINE)
===============================================================================

STEP 1:
    H1 = SHA256(header)

STEP 2:
    H2 = SHA256(payload)

STEP 3:
    H3 = SHA256(H1 || H2 || type_id)

STEP 4:
    H4 = Fold64(H3 XOR sequence_epoch XOR origin_cell_hash)

STEP 5:
    S_ECHO = SHA256(H4 || entropy_bound)

CONSTRAINT:
Execution order is strictly sequential and deterministic.

===============================================================================
CONSISTENCY LAW
===============================================================================

VALIDITY:

    S_A ≡ S_B ⇔ S_ECHO(RENORMALIZE(E_A)) == S_ECHO(RENORMALIZE(E_B))

INTERPRETATION:
- raw L1 state is not a comparison domain
- only invariant projection space is meaningful

===============================================================================
SMOKEPLATE EXECUTION MODEL
===============================================================================

Allowed:
- hardware-specific instruction scheduling
- SIMD divergence
- GPU kernel reordering
- memory layout variation

Forbidden:
- changes that alter S_ECHO result
- changes that alter RENORMALIZE output

Thus:

    Execution variability ∈ allowed set
    Identity drift ∉ allowed set

===============================================================================
ROLLBACK MODEL (ℛ)
===============================================================================

Rollback is deterministic replay:

    ℛ(S_t) = replay(L3_event_stream)

No snapshot restoration is permitted as truth.

===============================================================================
CONSENSUS MODEL (L5)
===============================================================================

Consensus is a convergence attractor:

    REALITY = fixed_point(S_ECHO(EVENT_SPACE))

Not voting.
Not majority.
Not probabilistic agreement.

Only stability convergence.

===============================================================================
SYSTEM GUARANTEE
===============================================================================

- deterministic replay across heterogeneous hardware
- invariant identity under resolution scaling
- tolerance to microstate noise (epsilon band)
- full causal reconstruction via L3 stream
- cross-engine compatibility via smokeplate abstraction

===============================================================================
FINAL SYSTEM STATEMENT
===============================================================================

DVSM defines computation as:

- event transformation over ordered causal space
- identity as renormalized invariant class
- truth as S_ECHO-stable equivalence structure
- execution as substrate-flexible deterministic kernel

Reality is not stored.

Reality is reconstructed.

